        "He returns you to the larger office as if the inner room had been a dream you both agreed to have. Your coat is on your shoulders again. The unused or emptied glass has been cleared. The folio is gone. The city is still there, sweating on schedule.\n\nA knock, precise. Marek does not wait to be adored. He opens, tablet already live. \"Director. The Vale packet for tomorrow, and Captain Radek wants a word about the east stair cameras. He says they blinked.\"\n\nCrowe does not look at you when he answers. \"Cameras blink when they are learning a new face. Tell Radek to let them learn. Rivers is leaving. Give them the south lift. The private one is tired.\"",
        "Marek's gaze flicks over your mouth, your collar, the place on your thigh that still feels like a stamp. He files. He smiles the aide smile. \"South lift. Of course.\"\n\nCrowe, at last, offers you his hand as if this had been a meeting about wellness. You take it. His grip is dry and brief and leaves the ghost of the thumb on your lip all over again. \"Tomorrow you will be useful,\" he says. \"Tonight you will be awake. Both are in my interest.\"\n\nHe has already turned to the Vale packet before you reach the door. Dismissal is a skill. He is better at it than at mercy, and he is very good at mercy when mercy is a hook.",
