        "You do not call. The decision feels like integrity and like cowardice and like the first private thing you have owned all week. You ride to your plate and walk the ventilation shaft to the slot that still smells of other people's cooking. The paper flower on the grate has lost a petal. You leave the petal on the floor because picking it up would be a domesticity you have not earned.\n\nYour phone lights. Voss: Report. Then, two minutes later: If you are dead I will be annoyed. Then nothing. Nothing is a leash she is choosing not to yank yet.\n\nYou sit on the bed that is also the sofa and look at your own thigh as if a palm print might still be there. Cloth holds nothing. Skin holds everything.",
        "Sleep, when it comes, is the clinic lighting again, too kind, and Crowe's voice saying tape as if it were a pet name. You wake once to the civic anthem leaking through the wall and you put your hand over your own mouth, not to silence a sound, to remember the shape of a thumb that may or may not have been invited.\n\nIn the morning you will steal or you will fail to steal. Tonight you keep the meeting in your body like a second PREP, a chemistry no vial authorized. The Stack writes rain on the grate. You do not answer Voss. You do not answer Mia. You answer, very quietly, the name Crowe used, just to hear whether it still belongs to you.",
